<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-RSH-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-RSH-001" ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T09:19:48Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S5 ;
  triage:title "Unbounded DNS resolution can stall the connection-worker pool" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs:495 (resolve_peer_address) calls to_socket_addrs() with no timeout, while every other stage on the same outbound path (connect/handshake/request) is explicitly bounded via HttpsRequestDeadline. A slow/unresponsive DNS server can block the calling thread indefinitely. FOLLOWUP (AICH-S5-FIX-1 recheck, a9e61fb0): NOT genuinely fixed — the bounded thread+mpsc::sync_channel+recv_timeout pattern was applied only to resolve_peer_addresses (plural, ~490-522), a helper used solely for literal-IP-to-hostname disambiguation inside resolve_peer_authority. The actual per-delivery resolver resolve_peer_address (singular, ~524-532), which HttpsTransport::deliver() calls at line 171 on every outbound peer delivery and every reconciliation replay (runtime_health.rs:681), remains completely unbounded. 4 independent reviewers converged on this exact fact during the recheck: rust-service-hardening-agent (Critical, unfixed), rust-best-practices-agent (cause-discarding also unfixed on this function, see AI25-RBP-F001), req-qa (ATM-QA-101, Blocking), arch-qa (consistent scope). RSH-002/RSH-003 sub-findings (O(N) fan-out only per-lookup bounded not aggregate-bounded; 5s reconciliation deadline still doesn't cover the resolver call inside deliver()) remain open for the identical root cause. The earlier fixed_partial/fixedOn-pAI-s26 status recorded on this finding was incorrect and is retracted by this update — the finding was never actually fixed on pAI-s25 or forward." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "AI25-RSH" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "closed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T10:54:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RSH-001/pAI-s25/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RSH-001/pAI-s25/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RSH-001/pAI-s25/3> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RSH-001/pAI-s25/4> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-RSH-001/pAI-s25/5> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/0265c94f> .

